<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7084"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:sugar@mhtc.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Mcattitude<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mcattitude<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 6:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->posted over at the eagle board and now they say that that yahoo group is on lockdown and no one can get in it. very interesting anyway read this. <BR> <BR>Im not sure if this is apporpriate but i am in a yahoo group and here is what precehr posted.....if it is not ok im sorry. Messages Messages Help  <BR> <BR>Reply | Forward | View Source | Unwrap Lines  <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>Message 809 of 809 | Previous | Next [ Up Thread ] Message Index Msg #  <BR> <BR> <BR>From: &#34;exhortist&#34; &#60;<a href="mailto:exhortist@y.">exhortist@y..</a>.&#62;  <BR>Date: Fri Feb 11, 2005 5:23 am  <BR>Subject: I know BTK, really! <BR> <BR> <BR>ADVERTISEMENT <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>This is the first of many posts that I plan to make concerning BTK. <BR>Being that I consider myself an &#39;average&#39; citizen of Wichita, Kansas <BR>I have heard about BTK. I was a senior in high school when he killed <BR>the four members of the Otero family. Being the &#39;normal&#39; self <BR>absorbed kid it didn&#39;t register much with me. I went off to college <BR>and never worried about it even when I came back to Wichita to get <BR>married and start a family. After the getting married and having a <BR>family didn&#39;t work out so well I was single again and living in <BR>Wichita. Having more bills than I could remember a single person <BR>having I started working second jobs to &#39;help&#39; with my &#39;bills&#39;. In <BR>some sort of rational way I started working in the bar scene. I say <BR>rational because I rationalized that I would be able to &#34;hang out&#39; <BR>where the singles were and make money instead of spending what I <BR>already couldn&#39;t afford. Needing to beat a dead horse is not my <BR>purpose in saying I met plenty of people. Wichita, just like any <BR>other large city has it&#39;s fair share of weirdos, wackos, flakes, <BR>freaks and psychopaths. I say that not meaning to insult my own <BR>hometown but as an observation having lived other places also. The <BR>big city is the best place for these people to hide out and find <BR>each other to feed off of. It may not seem like it but Wichita has <BR>been the biggest city around this area for the past fifty years or <BR>more. In the &#39;bar scene&#39; is where I met BTK. I actually hung out <BR>with a crowd or &#39;circle&#39; of people that he was a very manipulative <BR>part of. He came off as being a real hot-shot that knew way more <BR>than anyone else. He had a tendency in those days, the 80&#39;s, to pass <BR>him self off as a law enforcement type. Never being able to put up <BR>or shut up either one. That is how I know who he is. Let me <BR>elaborate. He liked to carry a Walther P-38 in a shoulder harness <BR>under his wool tweed jacket and wore jeans and cowboy boots. Much <BR>like an undercover but told many of the girls he was either CIA or <BR>DEA. The DEA part seemed plausible since he was always in the know <BR>on the &#39;coke scene&#39;. A very valuable &#39;knowlege&#39; in the 80&#39;s. He had <BR>a &#39;gold&#39; colored badge in a heavy leather badge wallet. He hardly <BR>ever got it out but had a tendency to get it out and give it a quick <BR>flip opened to closed under the nose of a drunk or seriously <BR>inebriated person while spouting in authoritative tones a line of bs <BR>meant to take that person off guard. I saw him do it a few times and <BR>it was very effective for him. I found the jacket to be interesting <BR>in retrospect as it was one of those with the leather patches on the <BR>sleeves at the elbows. A little dated for the 80&#39;s but highly <BR>favored amongst the college crowd in the early 70&#39;s where BTK was <BR>supposed to be impostering back then. It curiously is close now to <BR>the disclosures of Steve Relsford about his mothers attaker. BTK <BR>pulled his badge on me once at a private party. Not being much of a <BR>drinker even then I laughed at him and asked him why I would be <BR>afraid of &#39;the School Board Detective&#39;. Yes, unbelievably he reacted <BR>like no one had ever noticed that detail of his badge before. It <BR>made him so mad that when he slid it back into his pocket he came <BR>back out with a knife so fast even I couldn&#39;t believe how fast he <BR>had it at my jugular. He said &#34;ya know how easy I could kill you <BR>right now?&#34;. I could only reply, not easily enough or you&#39;d be doing <BR>and not talking. To which he only laughed pulling back and even <BR>letting me examine and hold the knife. Even then the touch of the <BR>knife had a chilling effect and I think he knew it. He only smiled. <BR>Sometime this summer an Article by Hurst Laviana in the Eagle about <BR>the package BTK sent to them had pictures of the stuff he sent. I <BR>believe it was the package of stuff he sent claiming Vicky Wegerles&#39; <BR>murder. There it was, that damn badge. I sort of dismissed it <BR>thinking that there could be other ones like it. A few days later <BR>Hurst wrote another article on a Sunday I believe asking people to <BR>ponder the new clues. &#34;Someone must know this person from the new <BR>clues&#39; then finnished the article by saying &#39;maybe someone from a <BR>small surrounding area town like Anthony.&#34; That&#39;s when it slammed me <BR>right up side the head. He had told me the story of when he was a <BR>kid in Anthony and how he had lifted that badge from the truant <BR>officer. Yes that night he showed it to me then bragged about how he <BR>got it. According to him it was his first &#39;trophy&#39; and was the first <BR>time he realized he had the power to &#39;trance&#39; people and take <BR>advantage of them. He claimed to have taken it right off the Truant <BR>Officer. I could tell back then that he meant it as a threat since <BR>the first two didn&#39;t work. I never was unduly afraid of this guy and <BR>just had forgotten about that incident until my memory was jogged by <BR>that story. That is partly the motivation for my expose&#39;. There are <BR>a lot of other things about this guy that will jog others memories <BR>when they hear them. I was amazed in retrospect how this guy fit <BR>when I actually knew who he was. I would have never guessed this was <BR>BTK, knowing him while evaluating his self-disclosed clues. That one <BR>braggadocious slip that he had forgotten about when he sent that <BR>badge. The fact he didn&#39;t think the WPD could trace the origin of <BR>it. The one slip that all criminals make and I saw it &#39;only by <BR>accident&#39; or as I believe, &#39;divine intervention&#39;. I hope this helps <BR>to answer whether or not the authorities know and if I think BTK <BR>knows who I am. My answer to both here again is yes. If he couldn&#39;t <BR>figure it out before he should know now.  <BR> <BR> <BR>  <BR> <BR>and this is about it being locked down now <BR> <BR>The moderator at the Yahoo! Group WichitaBTK has completely locked the group, it seems, as of this afternoon. <BR> <BR>I did read the same post Rockergirl replicated very early this morning while members still had access. <BR> <BR>All-in-all, very strange. <BR>  <BR>   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
