<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7087"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 6:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just a first impression hunch here. The poster claims he knows all kinds of BTK information; however, said data will be released &#34;in a series of posts.&#34; Okay, this guy doesn&#39;t contact LE, yet posts all this in a Yahoo discussion group. Additionally, his final sentence is <i>&#34;If he couldn&#39;t figure it out before he should know now.&#34;</i> That&#39;s a taunt, albeit a mild one. I think this is someone who is trying to imply that he is BTK, but isn&#39;t. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
