<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7095"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 7:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->They should follow-up anything; they have an IP number already. It just doesn&#39;t strike me as being BTK. Unless he&#39;s really become desperate. <BR> <BR>Just had a thought. Who has authority over Internet information? WPD, regardless? FBI?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
