<!--Post: 7098--><!--Time: 1108180822-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7098"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 8:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In any event, I&#39;m tired of people <i>posting</i> &#34;I know who BTK is&#34; or &#34;I have a lot of information about BTK which I alone know,&#34; without first having contacted the appropriate authorities.  <BR> <BR>Example: <i>I actually hung out  <BR>with a crowd or &#39;circle&#39; of people that <b>he was a very manipulative  <BR>part of.</b> He came off as being a real hot-shot that knew way more  <BR>than anyone else. <b>He had a tendency in those days, the 80&#39;s, to pass  <BR>him self off as a law enforcement type.</b> Never being able to put up  <BR>or shut up either one. <b>That is how I know who he is</b>.</i> <BR> <BR>Anyone who believes they know this much needs to contact LE. Go ahead and post, but notify LE first. Maybe the poster did notify LE but he should have said so if he had.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
