<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7121"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 1:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The poster&#39;s friend is an interesting suspect, but I agree with both George and NY - if you have a good suspect, contact LE first, even if you think they&#39;ll laugh you up good.  Not sure what to make of the badge thing - is he saying he saw a picture that matched his old buddy&#39;s badge?  Or just &#34;a badge&#34;?  The jacket is interesting - wasn&#39;t the sketched person seen near the Otero&#39;s wearing a similar jacket? <BR> <BR>My main doubt here is that this suspect sounds too socially successful.  He sounds plenty psychotic, but a bit too social.  Not bookish at all.  I can&#39;t imagine this guy being a pseudo-poet in a library.  I guess I&#39;ll have to wait for the next installment....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
