<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7125"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 3:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It sounds like this guy hung out in some rough bars and attended some rough parties. He might have found a crowd he could blend in with. I&#39;ve never heard of a bar owner who would tolerate guns in the place, permit or no permit. and apparently no one asked for a permit. <BR> <BR>Jackets with patches on the elbows always remind me of Mannix.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
