<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7133"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Fsu44<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Fsu44<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George is right, sounds good but reads like a &#34;True Detective&#34; story. Either way pass it on to LE. There was a tv show back in the 80&#39;s were this detective had a coat and a gun under his jacket: &#34;He liked to carry a Walther P-38 in a shoulder harness under his wool tweed jacket and wore jeans and cowboy boots on.&#34; I remember that show being on for may be one season. The location might have been Dallas or somewhere in Texas. The main actor was this  Magnum PI knock-off. Strange...Did the TV show &#34;Hunter&#34; dress this way also?  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
